    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490">

                <pb facs="0847" n="1805" xml:id="pg1805"/>

                <head>No. 35.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 2, 1888</date>.
                        (Received April 3.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Marquis of Salisbury has received intimation from the Canadian Government to the
                    effect that orders have been issued by the United States Government for the
                    capture of British ships fishing in Behring Sea, and that he has telegraphed to
                    me to represent earnestly the extreme importance of enabling Her Majesty’s
                    Government to contradict this rumor.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
